areer speaking  just walk on a stage once and once you  walk out there and you do the thing then  you have the confidence of I've done it  once I can do it again I didn't die from  it right exactly speaking thing people  think they're going about it does feel  like that sometimes but it's interesting  because if you can just do it once and I  tell people do it scared don't wait  until you're not scared to do the thing  you'll never do it just do it scared the  first time I walked on stage I was  scared and sometimes the second and  third times too but over time you look  back and go hey I've done it this many  times I've done these things I don't  have to be scared you have confidence of  experience to stand on but the first  time it is scary don't wait till you're  getting overcome the fear to do it just  do it scared do it anyway and then that  will make the fear dissipate just like  you said you know we've often everyone  has overused the metaphor of learning to  ride a bike but it's anytime you're  outside your comfort zone learning to do  something that's not going to kill you  right you know are not going to bring  you harm right and so you want to do it  scared but you don't want to do it  unwise and scared to where you know if  this doesn't work we bankrupt right we  don't do that right and so it's a it's a  baby step it's a small step but and what  we encourage folks to do is to take  positions that are if they fail it's a  non-fatal failure right and that reduces  the fear to where it's just an emotion  that's no longer a logical fear right  it's a logical fear that's telling you  not to touch a hot stove you want to  hear that one right now that tells you  don't step out in traffic you'll get run  over and so that's a logical fear but  the illogical fear that we all have on  man-woman new old entrepreneur whatever  it doesn't go away it just you learn to  control it and you learn to see it for  what it is and the way to beat that is  just do it anyway right and it's  interesting because a lot of times our  fears or a lot of the women I've spoken  to their fear is not around the plan the  business side of things their fears  around themselves what if I'm not good  enough what if I'm rejected what if we  what if I'm a failure and so it's a  large large it is it feels very  vulnerable so if you can help them over  that and then give them the tools to do  it wisely on the financial side and the  business side they've got both sides  that we need that they need very  interesting business boutique is the  event Christie right is the main speaker  Rachel Cruise Stephanie Parker cordilla  Arrington a whole lineup of top-flight  ladies in the business world there to  teach you about the different areas of  business learn about it at business  boutique comm are called triple a  22-piece triple eight two two seven  three two two three

